---
description: |
  Selects identifiers in a raw record that `demo::replay::run` renews in every
  cycle.

  ```tql
  demo::replay::renew_ids raw, "((?:session|parent)=)([0-9a-f]+)", kind="hex"
  demo::replay::run
  ```

  Within a cycle, equal identifiers stay equal across all records. The pattern
  must cover every place where an identifier occurs, or references to it break.
args:
  positional:
    - name: raw
      type: field
      description: The raw record.
    - name: pattern
      type: string
      description: Regular expression with two groups, the context to keep and the identifier to renew.
  named:
    - name: kind
      type: string
      description: |
        Layout of the identifier: `uuid`; `hex` with any number of digits;
        `number` with ten digits; or `pid`, which moves by one offset per cycle.
---

// The selection stays readable in the record until `demo::replay::run` renders
// it, for example `session=%%REPLAY%%renew:hex|1f3a9c20%%REPLAY%%`.
$raw = $raw.replace_regex($pattern, "\\1%%REPLAY%%renew:" + $kind + "|\\2%%REPLAY%%")
